<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 65,600 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 65,600 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 65,600 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Wednesday compared to 84,427 tonnes in the same period on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Wednesday   March 11</p>
<p>    Export cargo		23,425	26,589</p>
<p>    Import cargo		42,175	57,838</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, four ships sailed and six berthed. In the next 24 hours, five are expected to sail and eight are expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	  Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Crude oil		72,876	 Johar		  13/3</p>
<p>Palm oil		 12,000	 Wawasen Courage    15/3</p>
<p>Vehicles		 107	    Arcadia Highway    16/3</p>
<p>Containers		  240	 Dammam Bay	   19/3</p>
<p>Phosphate		29,887	 Lapanto Glory	20/3</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
